# pcapper .gitignore — ALLOW-LIST.
#
# pcapper is run from inside evidence directories and its outputs are, by
# design, unredacted: carved files, decrypted streams, recovered credentials,
# call audio, key logs, case exports. A deny-list has to anticipate every one
# of those; an allow-list only has to name the source tree. Everything is
# ignored unless a rule below un-ignores it. To ship a new kind of file, add
# it here on purpose.
#
# Check with:  git ls-files | git check-ignore --stdin --no-index   (prints nothing)
#              git status --ignored                                  (shows what is held back)

# 1. Ignore everything ...
*
# ... but let git descend into directories so the allow rules below can match.
!*/

# 2. Repository metadata and documentation
!.gitignore
!.gitattributes
!.github/**/*.yml
!.github/**/*.yaml
!LICENSE
!README.md
!SECURITY.md
!CHANGELOG.md
!CHANGELOG-archive.md
!docs/**/*.md

# 3. Packaging
!pyproject.toml
!requirements.txt

# 4. Source: the package and its shipped data tables
!pcapper/**/*.py
!pcapper/*.json

# 5. Tests: code, golden output, and the SYNTHETIC capture fixtures generated
#    by tests/make_fixtures.py (no real traffic). A real capture must never be
#    added here; put it under .local_tests/ (ignored) instead.
!tests/**/*.py
!tests/data/golden/*.txt
!tests/data/carve_gap.pcap
!tests/data/carve_wrap.pcap
!tests/data/dns.pcap
!tests/data/http.pcap
!tests/data/mixed.pcap
!tests/data/mixed.pcapng
!tests/data/modbus.pcap
!tests/data/tls.pcap
!tests/data/truncated.pcap
!tests/data/voip.pcap
!tests/data/voip_attack.pcap
!tests/data/voip_multiproto.pcap

# 6. Belt and braces. Everything below is already ignored by rule 1; these
#    rules exist so that a future, too-broad allow entry (say `!tests/data/*`)
#    still cannot commit key material, evidence or build output. Later rules
#    win, so keep this block last — and never add a pattern here that matches
#    an allow-listed file (`*.txt` would re-ignore the golden output).
#    tests/test_repo_hygiene.py fails if the tracked set ever drifts.

# Build, caches, environments, editors
__pycache__/
*.py[cod]
*$py.class
build/
dist/
*.egg-info/
.eggs/
.venv/
venv/
env/
.python-version
.pytest_cache/
.ruff_cache/
.mypy_cache/
.tox/
.nox/
.coverage
.coverage.*
coverage.xml
htmlcov/
.ipynb_checkpoints/
.idea/
.vscode/
*.swp
*.swo
*~
*.bak
*.orig
*.rej
.DS_Store
Thumbs.db
desktop.ini
.claude/
.local_tests/

# Captures. Bare *.pcap / *.pcapng are NOT repeated here: a later rule would
# re-ignore the twelve fixtures rule 5 allows (later rules win). Rule 1
# already ignores them everywhere else; tests/test_repo_hygiene.py checks
# that every tracked capture is one of the named fixtures and fixture-sized.
*.cap
*.pcap.gz
*.pcapng.gz
*.pcap.zst
*.pcapng.zst
*.pcap.xz
*.pcapng.xz
*.etl
*.erf
*.snoop

# pcapper outputs: carved / extracted / decrypted artifacts, recovered audio,
# case and evidence exports, run logs, IDS output.
carved/
decrypted/
extracted/
case-*/
files/
*.bin
*.wav
*.log
*.sqlite
*.sqlite3
*.db
*.csv
*.jsonl
*.ndjson
*.har
eve*.json
*.eve.json
suricata-*/
suricata_*/
*.zip
*.7z
*.rar
*.tar
*.tar.gz
*.tgz

# Key material, secrets and licensed databases
.env
.env.*
*.keylog
*keylog*.txt
sslkeys*.txt
*.pem
*.key
*.p12
*.pfx
*.crt
*.cer
*.der
*.mmdb
pcapper.toml
